# rudderstack_destination_snowflake_streaming (Resource)

This resource represents the Snowflake Streaming destination. For more information check
https://www.rudderstack.com/docs/destinations/streaming-destinations/snowflake-streaming/

## Example Usage

{{tffile "examples/destination_snowflake_streaming.tf"}}

> **:warning: Breaking Change**
> 
> Note that from the provider versions 5.0.0 and above, changing either `allow_users_context_traits` or `underscore_divide_numbers` forces a new destination to be created. Both are one-time flags that distinguish older destination behaviour from newer, and the control plane now rejects any update to them, so an in-place change could never succeed. Terraform replaces the destination instead — which assigns a **new destination ID**, so any connection pointing at it has to be re-pointed, and the warehouse will receive a different column set from the one it already holds. Plan carefully before changing either value on an existing destination.

